from reqs_rev4 import get,upd,acc,scen,test,new,REQS
from base import BG_TEAM
upd('REQ-012',statement=get('REQ-012')['statement']+' Each schema has an absolute `$id` (`urn:backlog:team-behaviour:2`, `urn:backlog:teams:2`, `urn:backlog:team-definition:2`, `urn:backlog:workflows:2`); a `$ref` to a sibling schema names that absolute `$id`, so a standard 2020-12 validator resolves it (R2-013). The subset adds `maxItems` and `maxProperties` (messages `must have at most <n> entries` / `must have at most <n> keys`). At the root of a file the `<path>: ` part of a message is omitted (R2-030).')
get('REQ-012')['scen']=[('S-012-1 dropped (R2-029)','Covered by T-012-1..T-012-3: the subset and the agreement of the two interpreters are not behaviour a user sees')]
test('REQ-012','engine-schema.test.js','python jsonschema and the JS interpreter agree on templates and schema/negative/*.json','tools/check_schemas.py','every template valid in both; every negative file invalid in both with the message of schema/negative/expected.tsv')
upd('REQ-013',statement=get('REQ-013')['statement']+' The numbered semantic rules are the table of `03-spec.md` §4.10 (V-01..V-40, E-01..E-11), each with its trigger and exact text; V-03 is withdrawn (D-26), V-27 is reduced to "a binding step needs to or to_rules" (D-25), V-29 is the required-key structural message, V-31..V-40 are new (R2-002, R2-005, R2-011, R2-012, R2-027, R2-032).')
upd('REQ-014',statement='The package ships `templates/team-behaviour/team.json` (= this plan\'s `templates/team.full.json`), `minimal.json`, `teams.example.json`, `workflows.example.json` (the two definitions inlined, generated from the first two) and the four schema files under `templates/team-behaviour/schema/`. Each template is valid; `team.json` reproduces today\'s team (§9, REQ-907). Templates are documentation and the input of `team workflow --file`/`team migrate`, never read at run time (REQ-003).',
 accept=['`backlog team validate --file <template:team.full.json>` and `--file <template:minimal.json>` exit 0 and print `✅ <path>: valid`; a unit test validates `teams.example.json` against `teams.schema.json` and `workflows.example.json` against `workflows.schema.json` (R2-019).',
 '`README.md` contains the four lines `templates/team-behaviour/team.json`, `templates/team-behaviour/minimal.json`, `templates/team-behaviour/teams.example.json`, `templates/team-behaviour/workflows.example.json` (checked by `docs-keys.test.js`, R2-020).'])
upd('REQ-015',statement='Machinery: `team define` refuses a changed entry of a team that has open items (`team <t> has <n> open items; register the new composition under another name`) and `team workflow --file` a changed definition used by teams with open items (`workflow <w> is used by teams with <n> open items; register the new flow under another name`); an item is open when its status is not a finished word of its own definition (R1-004); the refusals are configuration-command refusals: stderr `❌ backlog: <text>`, exit 2 (REQ-925 exception, R2-017). Upgrading a definition in use: CONDITIONAL on Q-20 (REQ-020).',
 accept=['With item 1 bound to t1 in `in progress`, `team define` of a changed t1 entry exits 2 with `❌ backlog: team t1 has 1 open items; register the new composition under another name` on stderr; with item 1 `closed` it succeeds.'])
# ---- new conditional requirements from the reviews (owner questions Q-16..Q-20)
new('REQ-016','Which workflow the running team uses after the migration','PH-1',['CFG-TEAMS'],
 'CONDITIONAL on Q-16. Option A (recommended): `backlog team migrate` writes `"workflow":"team"` into an entry without `workflow`; the converted `example-team` definition is registered for teams defined later; the live entry keeps the stage name `peer`. Option B: `backlog team migrate --workflow <team>=<name>` sets the entry\'s workflow in the migration commit (the only path that changes a team in use); the converted definition is the template with the stage renamed.',
 'R3-006: after the migration `team define` refuses to change a team with open items, so the choice is made inside the migration or not at all.',
 ['A: after `backlog team migrate` on a home whose entry t1 has no workflow, `teams.json` has `teams.t1.workflow` = `team`.','B: `backlog team migrate --workflow t1=example-team` gives `teams.t1.workflow` = `example-team` and the converted definition registered under `example-team`.'],
 [('A: an entry without workflow gets the template workflow','Given a repository with a backlog\n  And the file "teams.json" of the backlog home is `{"t1":{"lead":"lead","members":["ann"]}}`\nWhen I run `backlog team migrate`\nThen the command succeeds\n  And the file "teams.json" of the backlog home has the JSON value "team" at "teams.t1.workflow"')],
 [('team-migrate.test.js','Q-16 option A / B','schema 1 home','teams.t1.workflow = team (A) / example-team with the converted definition registered (B)')],'team-migrate',cond='Q-16')
new('REQ-017','Items bound to teams that have no entry','PH-1',['ST-LEGACY'],
 'CONDITIONAL on Q-17. Option A (recommended): the migration removes `team` from such items, keeps their status word as stored, and lists each under `unbound (team <t> has no entry)`. Option B: the migration aborts with `❌ backlog: <n> items are bound to teams without an entry: <team> (<k>: <slugs>); define each team (backlog team define) and run backlog team migrate again`.',
 'R3-009: twenty item files of the running backlog are bound to seven teams with no entry; no command can unbind them today.',
 ['A: an item bound to `ghost` loses `team` and appears in the migration output under `unbound (team ghost has no entry)`.','B: the migration exits 2 with the text of option B and writes nothing.'],
 [('A: an item of a team without an entry is unbound','Given a repository with a backlog\n  And an item "a" exists\n  And item 1 has the front-matter fields `{"team":"ghost","status":"done"}`\n  And the file "teams.json" of the backlog home is `{"t1":{"lead":"lead","members":["ann"]}}`\nWhen I run `backlog team migrate`\nThen the command succeeds\n  And the output contains "unbound (team ghost has no entry)"\n  And item 1 has field "team" equal to ""')],
 [('team-migrate.test.js','Q-17 option A / B','home with an item of team ghost','team removed and listed (A) / exit 2 with the listing text (B)')],'team-migrate',cond='Q-17')
new('REQ-018','Archived items with schema 1 fields','PH-1',['ST-LEGACY'],
 'CONDITIONAL on Q-18. Option A (recommended): the migration rewrites the front matter of archived items too (body untouched) and §8 names `team migrate` as the one writer allowed to change an archived item. Option B: archived items are left as stored; the old-item check of REQ-002 skips `archive/`, and readers show them as stored.',
 'R3-008: 24 bound archived files carry `stage`/`review_state`; the read-only rule and migrate-or-fail collide.',
 ['A: an archived item with `stage` loses it after the migration and `backlog show` of it exits 0.','B: the archived item is unchanged and `backlog show` of it exits 0 and prints `stage`.'],
 [('A: an archived item is migrated too','Given a repository with a backlog\n  And an item "a" exists\n  And item 1 has the front-matter fields `{"status":"closed","review_state":"passed"}`\n  And I run `backlog archive 1`\nWhen I run `backlog team migrate`\nThen the command succeeds\n  And I run `backlog show 1 --json`\n  And the output does not contain "review_state"')],
 [('team-migrate.test.js','Q-18 option A / B','home with an archived item with stage','front matter rewritten (A) / unchanged and readable (B)')],'team-migrate',cond='Q-18')
new('REQ-019','Split slices without a team','PH-1',['RF-JOIN'],
 'CONDITIONAL on Q-19. Option A (recommended): the migration binds every teamless slice whose parent is bound to the parent\'s team (with `refiner: ""`), and `backlog team new --split-from` always binds a slice; a slice outside a team is an ordinary item. Option B: teamless slices stay items outside a team; a team works them only after `--set-team`; the template offers none of them.',
 'R3-015 item 1: today a teamless slice is offered to the session\'s team and joins it on claim; the enforcer acts only on bound items (D-06).',
 ['A: a teamless slice of a bound parent is bound by the migration and offered by `team pop`.','B: the slice stays outside the team and `team pop` does not offer it.'],
 [('A: a teamless slice joins its parent\'s team','Given a repository with a backlog\n  And the backlog registers the workflow "team" from the template "team.full.json"\n  And a team "t1" with lead "lead" and members "ann, bob" using the workflow "team"\n  And an item "parent" exists\n  And item 1 has the front-matter fields `{"team":"t1","status":"new"}`\n  And an item "slice" exists\n  And item 2 has the front-matter fields `{"status":"pending","stage":"refining"}`\n  And item 2 body contains "Split from `001-parent`"\nWhen I run `backlog team migrate`\nThen the command succeeds\n  And item 2 has field "team" equal to "t1"')],
 [('team-migrate.test.js','Q-19 option A / B','home with a teamless slice of a bound parent','bound with refiner "" (A) / unchanged (B)')],'team-migrate',cond='Q-19')
new('REQ-020','Upgrading a definition used by teams with open items','PH-15',['DI-DEFINE-INUSE'],
 'CONDITIONAL on Q-20. Option A (recommended): `backlog team workflow --file` replaces a registered definition in use when every status word carried by an open item of its teams is a status of the new definition (and each item\'s review stage still exists); otherwise the REQ-015 refusal names the missing words. Option B: never (today): a changed definition is registered under a new name and teams move by `team define` once they have no open items.',
 'R3-006: a fix to the template found after the migration can otherwise never reach the running team.',
 ['A: a definition that adds a step registers while items are open; one that drops `refining` while an item is `refining` is refused with `workflow team is used by teams with 1 open items in words not in the new definition: refining`.','B: today\'s refusal.'],
 [('A: a compatible upgrade of a definition in use is registered','Given a repository with a backlog\n  And the backlog registers the workflow "team" from the template "team.full.json"\n  And a team "t1" with lead "lead" and members "ann, bob" using the workflow "team"\n  And I run `backlog team new --team t1 --agent lead --name a`\n  And a definition file "v2.json" from the template "team.full.json" with `description = "v2"`\nWhen I run `backlog team workflow --file v2.json`\nThen the command succeeds')],
 [('team-define-cli.test.js','Q-20 option A / B','team with an open item','compatible definition registered, incompatible refused naming the words (A) / refused (B)')],'team-file',cond='Q-20')
# ---- 10.1 statuses and steps
upd('REQ-101',statement='The words of a bound item are the `statuses` (and side words) of its definition; `initial` is the word of a new or newly bound item; a word in `finished` finishes the item for dependencies, the archive operations of the port and queue membership. No word is reserved: `backlog archive` moves the file and does not change `status`; an archived item is recognised by its path `archive/` only (D-26, R1-005).',
 accept=['With `minimal` registered for team m (`ready` → `in progress` → `closed`), `team update 1 --claim ann` then `--close --summary s` leaves item 1 with status `closed` (`backlog show 1 --json` field `status`).',
 'A definition whose `finished` is `["shipped"]` validates; `backlog archive 1` of a `shipped` item moves it to `archive/` and its status stays `shipped`.',
 '`backlog update 2 --status ready` of an unbound item stores `ready` and `backlog show 2` prints it; no team file is read (the guard test of REQ-905 proves the second half).'])
get('REQ-101')['scen']=[s for s in get('REQ-101')['scen'] if 'finished word of the definition lets' not in s[0]]
scen('REQ-101','a finished word of the definition lets a dependent go','Given a repository with a backlog\n  And the backlog registers the workflow "minimal" from the template "minimal.json" with `finished = ["closed","dropped","archived"] ; statuses = ["ready","in progress","closed","dropped","archived"] ; steps.claim.requires = [{"field_empty_or_actor":"claimed_by","refusal":"claimed_by_other"},{"dependencies_finished":{"handoff_states":null},"refusal":"dependencies_not_done"}] ; refusals.dependencies_not_done = "<item>: waits on <list>" ; refusals.dep_status = "<id> (<status>)" ; refusals.dep_foreign = "<id> (<repository>, <status>)" ; refusals.dep_missing = "<id> (missing)"`\n  And a team "m" with lead "lead" and members "ann, bob" using the workflow "minimal"\n  And I run `backlog team new --team m --agent lead --name p`\n  And item 1 has the front-matter fields `{"status":"dropped"}`\n  And I run `backlog team new --team m --agent lead --name d --depends-on 1`\nWhen I run `backlog team update 2 --team m --agent ann --claim ann`\nThen the command succeeds')
scen('REQ-101','an unfinished dependency blocks the claim of the patched definition','Given a repository with a backlog\n  And the backlog registers the workflow "minimal" from the template "minimal.json" with `steps.claim.requires = [{"field_empty_or_actor":"claimed_by","refusal":"claimed_by_other"},{"dependencies_finished":{"handoff_states":null},"refusal":"dependencies_not_done"}] ; refusals.dependencies_not_done = "<item>: waits on <list>" ; refusals.dep_status = "<id> (<status>)" ; refusals.dep_foreign = "<id> (<repository>, <status>)" ; refusals.dep_missing = "<id> (missing)"`\n  And a team "m" with lead "lead" and members "ann, bob" using the workflow "minimal"\n  And I run `backlog team new --team m --agent lead --name p`\n  And I run `backlog team new --team m --agent lead --name d --depends-on 1`\nWhen I run `backlog team update 2 --team m --agent ann --claim ann`\nThen the command fails with exit code 1\n  And the output contains "002-d: waits on 001-p (ready)"')
acc('REQ-104','`team update 1 --claim ann` of a `new` item under the template prints `❌ 001-a is new; claim needs ready or in progress` followed by the hint of `from_refusal_hints[0]` filled for item 1, exit 1 (the key list: `wrong_status`, `refine_first_hint`, `claim_awaiting_decision_hint`).',
 'Under a definition patched `steps.claim.from = ["new"]`, the same command on a `new` item succeeds; on a `ready` item it is refused with `wrong_status`.',replace=True)
acc('REQ-105','For each token of §6 step 13 (`same`, `previous`, `initial`, `first_review_stage`, `next_review_stage_if_satisfied`, `active_review_stage`, `flag_value`) a unit test gives the status after the step on a fixture item (T-105-1 lists the seven pairs); release under the template gives `reviewing` → `reviewing`, a slice `in progress` → `ready`, a work item `in progress` → `new` (R08).',replace=True)
acc('REQ-108','The template texts of `close_no_summary`, `refine_done_no_note`, `review_needs_comments` and `review_cite_refs` are printed filled for item 1 (old tests TST ids of `shared-team-lifecycle` and `shared-session-review` re-pointed, 05 §6).',replace=True)
upd('REQ-110',statement='At most one step without `combinable` per call (`one_step`, `<flags>` = the steps as `--name` in file order); `combinable` steps may accompany it and run first, in the order of `steps` in the file (no step name is special, D-25, R1-012); an `exclusive` step refuses accompanying edits (`edit_exclusive`).')
upd('REQ-111',statement='After a step (or verdict) with `ends_session`, unless the actor holds an excepted role, the last output line is `session.end_text` with `<agent>`; a verdict\'s `notice_rules` print the instruction of the first rule whose `when` holds on the item after the step, right after the update line (R1-011, R2-009).')
upd('REQ-113',statement='A definition may define a step with `"value": "word"` and `"to": "flag_value"`; the flag value must then be a word of `statuses` or `side_statuses`, else invalid input, exit 2: `❌ backlog: argument --<step>: invalid choice: \'<v>\' (choose from \'<w1>\', \'<w2>\', ...)` (words in file order). `--status` is an ordinary step name: the template defines no step `status` and maps it in `undefined_step_refusals` to `status_flag`, so today\'s refusal stays (D-25, R1-020, R2-007).')
acc('REQ-113','With a definition that adds `steps.status = {"value":"word","from":["*"],"to":"flag_value","by":["lead"]}`, `team update 1 --status gone` by the lead exits 2 with `argument --status: invalid choice: \'gone\' (choose from \'new\', ...)`.')
scen('REQ-113','a step to a word the definition does not have is invalid input','Given a repository with a backlog\n  And the backlog registers the workflow "team" from the template "team.full.json" with `steps.status = {"value":"word","from":["*"],"to":"flag_value","by":["lead"]} ; undefined_step_refusals = <delete>`\n  And a team "t1" with lead "lead" and members "ann, bob" using the workflow "team"\n  And I run `backlog team new --team t1 --agent lead --name a`\nWhen I run `backlog team update 1 --team t1 --agent lead --status gone`\nThen the command fails with exit code 2\n  And the output contains "argument --status: invalid choice: \'gone\'"')
upd('REQ-114',statement='When `session.block_after_end` is `{"field": "<f>"}`, a step with `ends_session` appends the caller session (Q-04) to the item field `<f>`, and every later step whose actor session is in `<f>` of any item of the home is refused with `session_ended`. Absent (template): nothing is recorded or checked (R1-010).')
